    fn chain(a: i64, b: i64, c: i64) -> bool { a < b < c }
    {"code": "E0211", "severity": "error", "message": "comparison operators cannot be chained", "file": "err/rust_habits.bmb", "line": 27, "col": 54, "end_line": 27, "end_col": 55, "fix": {"message": "split into two comparisons joined by `&&`"}}

Everything else the program prints must stay as it is.

